1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,060
The film was delivered and the office was behind them; the next deadline would be in another language.

2
00:00:06,060 --> 00:00:13,514
The fifth arc began with a journey: a plane, a truck, a jeep, and a tunnel in the same week.

3
00:00:13,514 --> 00:00:20,528
Aisha met them at the station with a thermometer in her bag and a pronunciation guide in her hand.

4
00:00:20,528 --> 00:00:25,567
“The tone of a language is part of its safety,” she said.

5
00:00:25,567 --> 00:00:33,492
“I is not the same as I am.” They themselves had left a service job for this.

6
00:00:33,492 --> 00:00:43,865
The big case was the rail line itself: a barrel of fluid, a coil of cable, and a cargo of berries had been waiting three days.

7
00:00:43,865 --> 00:00:49,979
The management of the rail service blamed the tide; the minister blamed the weather.

8
00:00:49,979 --> 00:01:04,643
“We survive by rumor here,” Aisha said, “and rumor is a rocky road.” We have to tell them that, and the night shift at the table was the position where the work of a year stood.

9
00:01:04,643 --> 00:01:12,806
The hope was a quiet one: that a small team could steal a march on a system with a billion reasons to ignore them.

10
00:01:12,806 --> 00:01:23,460
A football match on the platform, a piano playing jazz in the hall, and a drum and a whip in the market gave the place a rhythm they did not know.

11
00:01:23,460 --> 00:01:31,949
Him they watched most closely of all; itself, the station, kept its own time.

12
00:01:31,949 --> 00:01:35,643
The prime difficulty was not technical.

13
00:01:35,643 --> 00:01:41,898
“A mushroom grows overnight; a habit does not,” their host said.

14
00:01:41,898 --> 00:01:55,991
A pan, a chop, a knot of wire, and a ray of light through the carriage window: their host used objects to explain usage, and the therapy of it was patience.

15
00:01:55,991 --> 00:02:07,639
The hardship of the journey gave them a spur: a curl of paper with the timetable, a spit of rain on the glass, and the quiet endurance of a station cat.

16
00:02:07,639 --> 00:02:19,638
“They will treat us as tame,” Lin said, “until we are useful.” Aisha, who had created the timetable herself, said nothing.

17
00:02:19,638 --> 00:02:30,081
The king of the district had died that spring, and the station was still quiet; the journey home via the coast road was over before the fifth day.

18
00:02:30,081 --> 00:02:37,073
They would remember the tunnel, the tide, and the tone of a farewell for years.
